# Cursor Rules - [PROJECT_NAME]

**🔴 IMPORTANT: Load full AI instructions before responding to any command**

**When you read this file, immediately also read:**
→ `.exocortex/AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md` (contains all workflow commands and patterns)
→ `.exocortex/MEMORY.md` (project memory entry point)

This enables workflow commands to work in ANY editor (Cursor, VS Code, Claude Desktop).

## How This Works

**In Cursor:**
- Automatically reads this file on every response
- Automatically loads AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md (because this file tells it to)
- Commands work natively: /save, /work, /history, /groom, /daily-end, /scrum

**In VS Code / Other Editors:**
- Type once per conversation: "Read .cursorrules"
- AI reads this file → sees instruction to read AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md → loads everything
- Then commands work for entire session: work, save, groom, history, etc.

## Quick Command Reference

- `/save` - Save work event (append-only, no overwrites)
- `/work` - Load context and start working
- `/history` - Search older events (7+ days)
- `/groom` - Review and organize tasks
- `/daily-end` - End of day workflow
- `/scrum` - Daily standup

**Full instructions with detailed workflows:** `.exocortex/AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md`

---

## File Structure

```
.cursorrules                          # This file (pointer + quick reference)
.exocortex/
  ├── AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md              # Full workflow commands
  ├── MEMORY.md                       # Entry point to project memory
  ├── PROJECT_MEMORY.md               # System purpose, philosophy, constraints
  ├── SESSION_CONTEXT.md              # Current work (generated from events)
  ├── TODO.md                         # Task board
  ├── LESSONS.md                      # Project-specific lessons
  ├── events/                         # Append-only work events
  └── scripts/
      ├── generate_context.sh         # Regenerate SESSION_CONTEXT from events
      └── archive_events.sh           # Archive old events (7+ days)
```

---

## Emergency Recovery

If the AI seems to not know workflow commands:
1. Type: "Read .exocortex/AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md"
2. Confirm it loaded successfully
3. Then proceed with your command

